---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Responsible Play | Chancey"
  description="Responsible play guidance for Chancey users, including reminders about lottery odds and support resources."
>
  <article class="legal">
    <p class="eyebrow">Responsible play</p>
    <h1>Keep lottery play small and optional.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Lottery play involves real money and long odds. Chancey should be used for organization and convenience, not as a reason to spend more.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Set limits</h2>
      <p>
        Decide what you can afford before buying tickets and stop when you reach that limit. Do not use money needed for rent, bills, food, debt, or savings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Know the odds</h2>
      <p>
        Past draws do not guarantee future outcomes. Chancey number tools can help you choose faster, but they do not improve the odds of winning.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Get help</h2>
      <p>
        In the United States, call or text 1-800-GAMBLER for confidential help. Outside the U.S., contact a local problem-gambling support organization.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
